# [DIARIZE 29-Oct] Several people talk right after the call is picked up (family, shop,
# office), the caller among them. Learning "everything heard after the bot's question"
# mixed their voices into the caller's print. Now, before the lock, every ~1 s of voice
# gets a voice print; the prints are grouped into voices; each voice is scored by what
# only the CALLER does:
#   * answers the bot: speaks in the gap after (nearly) every bot line   (cov)
#   * listens while the bot talks: rarely speaks over the bot            (quiet)
#   * answers soon: within ~2.5 s of the bot stopping                    (early)
#   * is at the phone: louder than the other voices                      (level)
# The lock is learned from the best voice only when it clearly wins (DIARIZE_MARGIN).
# In doubt it waits, and after DIARIZE_MAX_WAIT_S of speech it falls back to the old
# rule — so the lock is never stuck. Customer audio to STT is NOT touched by this.
