# ── MUTE OTHER VOICE IN THE CUSTOMER'S TURN (v4.9) ────────────────────────────
# verify mode sends the caller's turn to STT untouched and judges the WHOLE turn
# afterwards — so a bystander talking in the middle of it got into the
# transcript, or made the whole turn (customer's words too) get dropped.
# With MUTE_OTHER, once the lock is PROVEN, every speech slice of a turn is also
# scored on its own ~1 s window; a window clearly not the customer
# (sim < MUTE_OTHER_SIM) is sent to STT as silence. Costs MUTE_LOOKAHEAD_HOPS
# x 100 ms of extra delay on the caller's audio (only after the lock is proven).
# Tested (12-Oct, 3 speaker sets, real 8 kHz voices, all male = the hard case):
# on a quiet line about half of a bystander's speech is silenced and 1-2 % of
# the customer's (up to ~13 % right where the voices change). Under loud babble
# / AC the customer's own 1 s windows scored 0.03-0.17 and 43 % of them would
# have been cut — so it switches itself off when the line is noisy
# (MUTE_MAX_NOISE_RATIO). A slice is muted when
#     sim < MUTE_OTHER_SIM,  or  sim < MUTE_PITCH_SIM and its pitch is
#     >= MUTE_PITCH_ST semitones away from the customer's (e.g. man vs woman).
MUTE_OTHER          = _b("MUTE_OTHER", False)
MUTE_OTHER_SIM      = _f("MUTE_OTHER_SIM", 0.20)
MUTE_PITCH_SIM      = _f("MUTE_PITCH_SIM", 0.30)
MUTE_PITCH_ST       = _f("MUTE_PITCH_ST", 4.0)
MUTE_OTHER_HYST     = _f("MUTE_OTHER_HYST", 0.05)     # unmute needs sim >= SIM + this
MUTE_MAX_NOISE_RATIO = _f("MUTE_MAX_NOISE_RATIO", 0.15)  # line floor / customer level
MUTE_MIN_S          = _f("MUTE_MIN_S", 0.5)           # shorter windows are never muted
MUTE_LOOKAHEAD_HOPS = _i("MUTE_LOOKAHEAD_HOPS", 2)


